SUMMARY:Jordan: Social security contributions payment to the Social Securit
 y Corporation
DESCRIPTION:The firm must pay the contributions deducted from its insured w
 orkers and those it pays for them during the first 15 days of the month af
 ter they fall due. Default interest of 1% per month applies to overdue con
 tributions.\nApplies to: Firms (employers) with insured workers under the 
 Social Security Law\nNon-working-day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: ht
 tps://www.ssc.gov.jo/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/law-26.1.2025-compressed.p
 df\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#jordan\n\nFo
 r information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring r
 ule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources 
 last checked 12 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#jordan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
